tickets.what:
`docs/spec.md` §2.2 & `.scratch/panel-v2/spec.md` §5. Show fast, safe per-file `--numstat` diff summaries with proportional `+ / -` bars when reviewing To-try slices, inspecting a job's worktree/commits, or viewing Working tree changes.

  - Working tree dirty diff (`git diff HEAD --numstat`) for `ProjectCollector`'s `tree` page;
  - Commit/range diff (`git show --numstat --format=` across the 1–5 commit hashes named on a `try` ledger slice);
  - Job diff (`BASE..HEAD` plus working tree in `job.worktree.root` or `SESSION.txt` `BASE` when available) for Inspector.

`docs/spec.md` §2.2 & `.scratch/panel-v2/spec.md` §6. Give the Control plane proactive visibility into client quota watermarks, today's pi spend, and today's per-role dispatch health so the owner can switch presets before hitting walls.

  - Client quotas: read latest known Claude / Codex quota percentages & reset times from `$HUD_HOME/display/state/*.json` snapshots when fresh (never invoking network calls);
  - Pi today spend: sum today's input/output tokens and cost (when recorded in pi session headers/entries under `~/.pi/agent/sessions` or HUD display cache, bounded to today's modified files);
  - Today's role health: scan newest 200 `$HUD_HOME/jobs` created today (local TZ) to tally per-role `{ total, ok, failed, quiet_escalated, avg_minutes }`.

`docs/spec.md` §2.2 & `.scratch/panel-v2/spec.md` §7. Export a rich, zero-server, single-file static HTML board for reviewing project progress, To-try slices (briefs, steps, linked tickets, diff bars), active jobs and milestone reviews in a browser.

  - Strictly escape all untrusted/external text (`& < > " '`), zero external fonts/scripts/stylesheets/fetches (`Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'`);
  - Responsive CSS (works from phone width up to wide desktop) with automatic `prefers-color-scheme` + a pure-CSS light/dark toggle (matching `docs/design/panel-v8/` craft);
  - Sections: Header (project, branch, milestone stacked bar & counts), Waiting for Owner & Open Job Questions, To-Try Review Queue (cards with model brief, numbered acceptance steps, linked `.scratch/` ticket checklists, and `--numstat` diff bars), Active Workers, and Latest Milestone Review.
